siren (0.12.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * MAJOR CHANGES:
    - Message sending is now MUCH faster
    - Application starts quicker
    - Bug fix: illegal characters in messages caused silent failures
    - New: refuse to send to duplicate phone numbers
    - New: verify that the "from" phone number is associated with the account
  * Technical details:
    - Complete rewrite from C++/Pascal to pure C++ with wxWidgets
    - Updated config file format to simple JSON
    - Normalize messages LIVE (in-window) to the GSM character set
    - Sign in to Twilio asynchronously on startup rather than blocking
      (This is why the application starts instantaneously now)
    - Normalize phone numbers to E.164 format automatically
    - Send messages as fast as we can, and employ an exponential backoff if
      we receive a 429 "too many requests" response from Twilio
      The old Pascal implementation had an arbitrary wait between messages to
      avoid hitting Twilio's rate limits: this approach is MUCH faster

 -- rail5 <andrew@rail5.org>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 10:18:45 +0800

